A||||3||theogre||Tip: Weather Pack Connectors||||1||
Z||000000||theogre||01-14-2001||04:25 PM||||To be added to the ever evolving wiring article in the ECM section of my Fiero Cave....<P><B>WARNING!</B> This only applies to Weather Pack terminals. The O2 sensor, the MAP sensor, and some others are Weather Pack. (The 86&up trunk harness by the battery is Weather Pack. All Weather Pack have this same look.)<P>Are the latches on your Weather Pack connectors broken? Did You know many of the Weather Pack connector shells are available at Pep Boys and many other parts stores?<P>The question is How do you get the old shell off. That's actually quite simple. cut it off carfully with wire cutters. It usually cracks apart in big chunks. Be careful not to damage the wire or the seal on the wire.<P>Once the old connector is gone, simply slide the terminal and seal into the new shell until it clicks locked and close the back cover. That's all there is to it. (I just fixed my busted O2 sensor connector today. took less than 10 minutes.)<P>It is important that you keep the O2 sensor connector in good shape. If that terminal is crappy you'll take a hit in performance and gas millage. The new shell for the car side of the O2 connection is about $1.50, very cheap insurance.<P>You can also get pre made ends with pigtails. This is handy if the terminal or wire is broken. (These are available for many common connectors, not just Weather Pack.)<P>This shell replacement WILL NOT WORK for the newer style TPS, ECT, MAT, DIS Brick, and other high density connectors. These new connectors are GT or Metri Pack connectors. While they use seals similar to Wether Pack they do not assemble the same way.<P>you can find more information on the various connectors in my cave. <P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||01-15-2001||05:19 PM||||Thanks, Ogre - a very timely tip, for me, at least.  My current project seems to be breaking off the locking tabs on about 1 out of every 4 connectors I fool with, on my GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">.  They seem to be getting brittle in their old age - hopefully, I won't get that way over the years, too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">        ||||reg||10
Z||000002||theogre||01-15-2001||07:37 PM||||it is also posible to release a terminal from a good shell w/o breaking it. But that will be put into the wiring article. I need a diagram or two to describe the process.<P>This is important when the connector is good but one wire has been broken. Also allows the use of scavenged Weather Pack shells if one turns out to be unavailable in the store.<P>This won't work on GT and Metri Pack connectors. The only way most people are going to be able to fix those is if you get a good connector with leads and splice it on the harness. Some of these are available prefab in the parts store. others will have to be scavenged.<P>I have the same problem in my 87SC. The biggest enemy of all these connectors is long term exposeure to excesive heat. If you check out other cars the same age many of the connectors are in quite good shape.<P>This is yet another symptom of Fiero's heat management problem. (read the snake charming thread to see some of how it relates to belts.) One of the things I'll be checking out in spring is Techline Coatings. They have coatings along the line of what Jet Hot does. For $20 for enough to do the exhaust manifold it's worth a try. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-16-2001||08:47 PM||||I finally identified the newer ECT, MAT, TPS, etc. connectors used on 87 and up 4 cylinder. maybe late model V6's as well.<P>They are Metri-Pack 150.2 Pull-to-Seat connectors. (Made by Delphi Packard division of Delphi Automotive.) These things are a real pain in the ass to fix. Best thing to do with them is cut it off and splice a good one on. The terminals can be replaced but getting the extra terminals is a _____. Getting the bad one out isn't any fun either.||||reg||1
